---
title: Macaroni and Cheese
servings: 4
time: 45 min
tags: pasta, cheese, comfort-food, dinner, vegetarian
cuisine: American
course: main
source: mac_and_cheese.png
---

Preheat oven to 375°F (190°C).

Cook @macaroni{8%oz} in boiling water for ~{6%minutes} and drain.

Coat a #baking dish{} with @butter spray{} and transfer the drained macaroni into the dish.

In a #saucepan{}, whisk together @all-purpose flour{1/8%cup}, @dry mustard{1/4%tsp}, @black pepper{1/8%tsp}, and @milk{1 1/4%cups} until smooth.

Cook over medium heat, stirring constantly, until the sauce thickens (~{10%minutes}).

Stir in @cheddar cheese{3/4%cup}(grated) until completely melted and smooth. Pour cheese sauce over the macaroni and mix well.

Top with @bread crumbs{1/8%cup} and remaining @cheddar cheese{1/4%cup}(grated).

Bake at 375°F for ~{25%minutes} until the topping is lightly browned and bubbly.
